<title>USA: McDonald's seen growing 15 pct/yr-BARRON'S.</title>
<headline>McDonald's seen growing 15 pct/yr-BARRON'S.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>While several analysts have lowered their earnings projections and/or their investment recommendations of McDonald's Corp recently, Dick Strong of the Strong Funds has a favorable view of the stock, according to Barron's.</p>
<p>&quot;I think McDonald's stock will reflect the fact that earnings per share should grow 15 percent a year over the next five years,&quot; said Strong in the Barron's report.</p>
<p>He said that 10 years from now, the companay is predicted to have less than 35 percent of its earnings coming from domestic operations, compared to 46 percent now.</p>
<p>McDonald's stock closed at 44-5/8 Friday.</p>
